		{"id":"a600f5671fc0350b","type":"text","text":"### Trait impl via [[Response]]","x":-134,"y":-620,"width":293,"height":50,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"36f681abf9b7b82a","type":"text","text":"### `proc-macro` provides [[hurtbreak-cli|CLI]] implementation","x":-500,"y":492,"width":472,"height":50,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"de300e38d4b86bd0","type":"text","text":"### [[hurtbreak-derive]] provides mutation methods","x":-8,"y":492,"width":500,"height":50,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"55ef79ae288674f6","type":"text","text":"## Exposed to [[hurtbreak-c]] ","x":-620,"y":592,"width":209,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"8d76204e642f3e42","type":"text","text":"### Methods in [[hurtbreak-core]] and [[Attack|Attack (trait)]] are provided to the end user, intaking the struct\n- This would be a generic of [[Fuzzable]]","x":-133,"y":672,"width":375,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0f3afeb06026cb8c","type":"text","text":"## Exposed to [[hurtbreak-py]] ","x":-620,"y":852,"width":209,"height":84,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"fee1e9e9104ba39c","type":"text","text":"#### Define data structure in C instead","x":-880,"y":300,"width":290,"height":75,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"9ec44d291b57eb55","type":"text","text":"### Trait impl via [[Fuzzable]]","x":-145,"y":312,"width":275,"height":50,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0f63a303c51131df","type":"text","text":"# End User Tool","x":-112,"y":-320,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"3de4fd51f49705c4","type":"text","text":"### Trait impl for attack flow via [[Tripwire]]","x":-112,"y":-780,"width":250,"height":73,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"e91b7be51b97fba7","type":"text","text":"## Exposed to [[hurtbreak-py]] ","x":-880,"y":-903,"width":209,"height":84,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e18c6523559e1c01","type":"text","text":"### Input is mutated using [[Fuzzable]] on a per field basis guided by [[Tripwire]]","x":-540,"y":-971,"width":303,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"fc56b490c83bfb07","type":"text","text":"##### Every mutation produces an [[RNG]] seed that can reproduce the mutation. When the next step in the attack flow (via [[Tripwire]]) is reached, the seed of the generation is added onto the previous step's seed.\n- For example, if the attack is seed `ABC`, `DEF`, `GHI`, the output seed in logs would be `ABC_DEF_GHI`.","x":-102,"y":-1111,"width":480,"height":205,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"78525f2dde6d03d8","type":"text","text":"## Exposed to [[hurtbreak-c]] ","x":-880,"y":-1008,"width":209,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"e4df4bfb674531b0","type":"file","file":"hurtbreak-trace.md","x":840,"y":-903,"width":640,"height":515,"color":"6"}
	],
